,"death":null},"Q5528031":{"label":"Željka Cvijanović","description":"Bosnian Serb politician","enwiki":"Željka Cvijanović","summary":"Željka Cvijanović (née Grabovac; Serbian Cyrillic: Жељка Цвијановић, née Грабовац, pronounced [ʒêːʎka tsʋijǎːnoʋitɕ]; born 4 March 1967) is a Bosnian Serb politician who has served as the Serb member of the Presidency of Bosnia and Herzegovina since 2022. She previously served as president of Republika Srpska from 2018 to 2022.\nA member of the Alliance of Independent Social Democrats, Cvijanović was prime minister of Republika Srpska from 2013 to 2018. In the 2018 general election, she was elected president of Republika Srpska, assuming office on 19 November 2018.","image":"Željka Cvijanović (2024-12-18).jpg","birth":1967.1698630136987,"death":null},"Q297825":{"label":"Željko Komšić","description":"Bosnian Croat politician","enwiki":"Željko Komšić","summary":"Željko Komšić (Croatian pronunciation: [ˈʒɛːʎkɔ ˈkɔmʃitɕ]; born 20 January 1964) is a Bosnian politician who has served as the Croat member of the Presidency of Bosnia and Herzegovina since 2018, having served from 2006 to 2014 as well. Previously, he was a member of the national House of Representatives from 2014 to 2018.\nBorn in 1964, Komšić earned a degree in law from the University of Sarajevo in 1988, and later attended a specialization program at Georgetown University. He served in the Army of the Republic of Bosnia and Herzegovina during the Bosnian War, and was awarded with the Order of the Golden Lily.","image":"Željko Komšić (2025-12-17) (cropped).jpg","birth":1964.051912568306,"death":null},"Q387491":{"label":"Borjana Krišto","description":"Chairwoman of the Council of Ministers of Bosnia and Herzegovina since 2023","enwiki":"Borjana Krišto","summary":"Borjana Krišto (née Krželj; born 13 August 1961) is a Bosnian Croat politician who has served as Chairwoman of the Council of Ministers of Bosnia and Herzegovina since January 2023. She previously served as president of the Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina from 2007 to 2011. She is the first woman to hold both positions.\nKrišto holds a degree in law from the Faculty of Law at the University of Banja Luka.","image":"Borjana Krišto (2025-06-11).jpg","birth":1961.613698630137,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Bosnia and Herzegovina.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Flag_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg","author":"Mladen Kolobarić","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Bosnia and Herzegovina.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coat_of_arms_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg","author":"See File history below for details.","license":"Public domain"},"Denis Bećirović - March 2026.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Denis_Be%C4%87irovi%C4%87_-_March_2026.jpg/330px-Denis_Be%C4%87irovi%C4%87_-_March_2026.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denis_Be%C4%87irovi%C4%87_-_March_2026.jpg","author":"© European Union 2026","license":"Attribution"},"Željka Cvijanović (2024-12-18).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%C5%BDeljka_Cvijanovi%C4%87_%282024-12-18%29.jpg/330px-%C5%BDeljka_Cvijanovi%C4%87_%282024-12-18%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%BDeljka_Cvijanovi%C4%87_(2024-12-18).jpg","author":"European Union","license":"Attribution"},"Željko 